527
00:20:07,288 --> 00:20:08,987
- So you want to give us nicknames. - We need to come up with it.

528
00:20:08,988 --> 00:20:11,158
- We need to come up with it. - Like what?

529
00:20:11,958 --> 00:20:13,628
For example, Kkyu.

530
00:20:14,988 --> 00:20:16,797
(Kkyu)

531
00:20:16,798 --> 00:20:18,057
- "Kkyu" sounds good. - "Kkyu" sounds good.

532
00:20:18,058 --> 00:20:19,797
- He likes that nickname. - Kkyu.

533
00:20:19,798 --> 00:20:21,327
- Kkyu, yaho. - Kkyu.

534
00:20:21,328 --> 00:20:23,938
Or how about this?

535
00:20:24,368 --> 00:20:26,438
Kkyu and Jjyu.

536
00:20:26,638 --> 00:20:28,237
- Kkyu-Jjyu. - Kkyu-Jjyu?

537
00:20:28,238 --> 00:20:30,307
- Yes. Kkyu and Jjyu. - Why Jjyu?

538
00:20:30,308 --> 00:20:32,747
- What's Jjyu? - Because his name is Seo Jin.

539
00:20:32,748 --> 00:20:34,547
- Jjyu? - It's the J.

540
00:20:34,548 --> 00:20:36,148
- Jjyu? - "It's the J."

541
00:20:37,018 --> 00:20:39,087
- My gosh. - His name has a J in it, so Jjyu?

542
00:20:39,088 --> 00:20:42,048
- It sounds good. - It sounds like a dog name.

543
00:20:42,218 --> 00:20:44,457
- Jjyu. - Jjyu.

544
00:20:44,458 --> 00:20:46,428
That's what you say when you call a dog.

545
00:20:46,758 --> 00:20:48,488
- Jjyu. - Jjyu.

546
00:20:50,858 --> 00:20:54,427
(Today's secretaries are Kkyu and Jjyu.)

547
00:20:54,428 --> 00:20:56,638
So what are we doing here today?

548
00:20:56,968 --> 00:20:59,337
- It's a commercial. - It's a commercial.

549
00:20:59,338 --> 00:21:01,937
You should keep checking on us.

550
00:21:01,938 --> 00:21:03,207
Make sure we eat properly.

551
00:21:03,208 --> 00:21:04,537
- I'm hungry. - Food is very important.

552
00:21:04,538 --> 00:21:06,447
I'm starving.

553
00:21:06,448 --> 00:21:08,247
Since we're doing a group shoot soon,

554
00:21:08,248 --> 00:21:10,047
- should we order food in advance? - Let's do that.

555
00:21:10,048 --> 00:21:11,547
- What do you want? - Great.

556
00:21:11,548 --> 00:21:12,717
- It's a brilliant idea. - What do you want?

557
00:21:12,718 --> 00:21:15,017
- Are you a genius? - Can you...

558
00:21:15,018 --> 00:21:17,057
- Kkyu-Jjyu. - Kkyu-Jjyu.

559
00:21:17,058 --> 00:21:18,827
We want to eat malatang.

560
00:21:18,828 --> 00:21:20,087
- Malatang. - Malatang?

561
00:21:20,088 --> 00:21:22,557
- Malatang! - No, you'll gain weight.

562
00:21:22,558 --> 00:21:23,658
Why not?

563
00:21:25,968 --> 00:21:30,467
(Kkyu surprisingly gave a cold refusal.)

564
00:21:30,468 --> 00:21:33,367
We'll resume the photoshoot. I'm sorry.

565
00:21:33,368 --> 00:21:35,537
- Okay. - Is it a group shoot now?

566
00:21:35,538 --> 00:21:36,778
Yes.

567
00:21:37,338 --> 00:21:38,737
Who wants to eat malatang?

568
00:21:38,738 --> 00:21:40,307
(He quickly takes orders before the photoshoot.)

569
00:21:40,308 --> 00:21:41,777
Do you just want malatang?

570
00:21:41,778 --> 00:21:43,118
I want to eat seolleongtang.

571
00:21:43,578 --> 00:21:45,888
- Then... - Are you really from Japan?

572
00:21:46,048 --> 00:21:47,787
I'll join you then.

573
00:21:47,788 --> 00:21:48,917
- Do you want seolleongtang too? - Yes.

574
00:21:48,918 --> 00:21:51,487
So 2 bowls of seolleongtang and 2 bowls of malatang?

575
00:21:51,488 --> 00:21:53,257
- Yes. That's perfect. - Is that all you need?

576
00:21:53,258 --> 00:21:55,427
- Please add fen hao zi. - Sorry?

577
00:21:55,428 --> 00:21:56,728
Please add fen hao zi.

578
00:21:57,128 --> 00:21:59,568
- To the malatang. - What's fen hao zi?

579
00:22:00,728 --> 00:22:01,928
Don't you know what it is?

580
00:22:02,338 --> 00:22:04,037
- Is it for malatang? - Yes.

581
00:22:04,038 --> 00:22:05,808
- Glass noodles too. - Fen hao zi.

582
00:22:06,238 --> 00:22:07,338
Fan hao zi?

583
00:22:07,468 --> 00:22:09,337
Is it "fan" or "fen?"

584
00:22:09,338 --> 00:22:10,608
- Fen. - Fen hao zi?

585
00:22:11,938 --> 00:22:14,747
"Fen hao zi."

586
00:22:14,748 --> 00:22:17,047
(He doesn't know what it is, but he writes it down.)

587
00:22:17,048 --> 00:22:18,518
So what do you want to add?

588
00:22:18,778 --> 00:22:19,988
Fen hao zi.

589
00:22:20,088 --> 00:22:21,747
Fen hao zi...

590
00:22:21,748 --> 00:22:23,117
- and mung bean sprouts. - Mung bean sprouts?

591
00:22:23,118 --> 00:22:24,458
Kwang Kyu, please add that.

592
00:22:24,888 --> 00:22:26,387
- But the basic ingredients are... - There are...

593
00:22:26,388 --> 00:22:27,887
a lot of basic ingredients.

594
00:22:27,888 --> 00:22:29,398
- You should add them all. - Mung bean sprouts?

595
00:22:29,728 --> 00:22:31,358
- Yes. - Gosh. Kwang Kyu.

596
00:22:31,728 --> 00:22:32,767
Mung bean sprouts?

597
00:22:32,768 --> 00:22:34,798
Tell us everything.

598
00:22:35,298 --> 00:22:37,638
- It'd be better to check. - Yes.

599
00:22:38,168 --> 00:22:40,207
- Let us add it. - Fen hao zi, mung bean sprouts.

600
00:22:40,208 --> 00:22:42,477
- Let us add it. - Not seolleongtang.

601
00:22:42,478 --> 00:22:44,407
- Yes. - Two servings of malatang?

602
00:22:44,408 --> 00:22:45,707
- Yes. - Isn't two servings a bit much?

603
00:22:45,708 --> 00:22:47,448
- It's 2 servings, level 1.5. - It's okay.

604
00:22:48,078 --> 00:22:49,577
- Is it the spiciness level? - Is it the spiciness level?

605
00:22:49,578 --> 00:22:50,578
Yes.

606
00:22:50,818 --> 00:22:53,218
- So they have different levels. - Let's add more.

607
00:22:54,148 --> 00:22:56,357
- Wood ear. - And cabbage.

608
00:22:56,358 --> 00:22:57,918
Do you eat wood ear too?

609
00:22:58,018 --> 00:22:59,057
Cabbage.

610
00:22:59,058 --> 00:23:00,988
- Cabbage? - Wood ear.

611
00:23:01,058 --> 00:23:02,058
(Laughing in disbelief)

612
00:23:02,088 --> 00:23:03,227
Dried tofu.

613
00:23:03,228 --> 00:23:04,497
- Dried tofu. - You guys will gain weight.

614
00:23:04,498 --> 00:23:06,197
- Dried tofu? - You guys eat a lot.

615
00:23:06,198 --> 00:23:07,268
Potato.

616
00:23:07,428 --> 00:23:09,438
- Really? - Your company treats you guys well.

617
00:23:10,098 --> 00:23:11,368
Cheesy rice cake?

618
00:23:11,768 --> 00:23:12,768
(The Japanese member is taking notes.)

619
00:23:12,769 --> 00:23:15,007
(Mung bean sprouts, cabbage, wood ear mushroom, enoki mushroom,)

620
00:23:15,008 --> 00:23:17,278
(dried tofu, Chinese glass noodles)

621
00:23:17,578 --> 00:23:18,837
- Yes. - Can you fit...

622
00:23:18,838 --> 00:23:20,108
all these ingredients into two servings?

623
00:23:21,478 --> 00:23:22,847
- That's... - And...

624
00:23:22,848 --> 00:23:24,477
- Snow ear. - Small napa cabbage.

625
00:23:24,478 --> 00:23:25,517
Chinese glass noodles.

626
00:23:25,518 --> 00:23:27,587
(It's a new world to him.)

627
00:23:27,588 --> 00:23:30,217
Can we begin the photoshoot now?

628
00:23:30,218 --> 00:23:31,317
- Yes. - Yes.

629
00:23:31,318 --> 00:23:33,327
- Hurry up and go. - Let's go.

630
00:23:33,328 --> 00:23:34,887
- Go now. - Put on your shoes.

631
00:23:34,888 --> 00:23:35,957
It's fine. We should...

632
00:23:35,958 --> 00:23:37,927
- I caught a cold. - Okay.

633
00:23:37,928 --> 00:23:40,097
Can you give me some medicine after I eat?

634
00:23:40,098 --> 00:23:42,537
- Sure. - We have cold medicine.

635
00:23:42,538 --> 00:23:44,268
- All right. - Are you done?

636
00:23:44,498 --> 00:23:45,867
- Thank you. - Is everything okay?

637
00:23:45,868 --> 00:23:46,868
- Okay. - Let's go.

638
00:23:48,038 --> 00:23:52,408
(Their first task is to prepare lunch.)

639
00:23:52,808 --> 00:23:54,748
Will all these ingredients fit into two servings?

640
00:23:55,308 --> 00:23:56,917
- What? - Will these fit into two servings?

641
00:23:56,918 --> 00:23:59,147
(Malatang with 12 ingredients)

642
00:23:59,148 --> 00:24:01,017
- Two bowls of seolleongtang? - Yes.

643
00:24:01,018 --> 00:24:02,788
"Fen hao zi malatang." Is this what they were talking about?

644
00:24:05,088 --> 00:24:06,128
"Fen..."

645
00:24:06,928 --> 00:24:08,788
What's fen hao zi?

646
00:24:09,498 --> 00:24:10,698
"Fen hao zi."

647
00:24:11,328 --> 00:24:12,827
- It's fen hao zi malatang, right? - Yes.

648
00:24:12,828 --> 00:24:14,067
That's what they wanted.

649
00:24:14,068 --> 00:24:16,097
Didn't they tell us to add fen hao zi to their malatang?

650
00:24:16,098 --> 00:24:17,168
(Confused)

651
00:24:17,498 --> 00:24:19,838
They wanted to order fen hao zi malatang.

652
00:24:21,908 --> 00:24:22,937
I don't know.

653
00:24:22,938 --> 00:24:24,207
(I have no idea.)

654
00:24:24,208 --> 00:24:26,777
I should look up what "fen hao zi" is.

655
00:24:26,778 --> 00:24:28,048
(He looks up what "fen hao zi" is before ordering delivery.)

656
00:24:28,448 --> 00:24:30,218
This is fen hao zi.

657
00:24:30,648 --> 00:24:33,387
- It's like rice cake. - I added it.

658
00:24:33,388 --> 00:24:34,517
You did?

659
00:24:34,518 --> 00:24:36,858
I thought fen hao zi was like the hat I wear.

660
00:24:39,228 --> 00:24:40,388
"Hao zi" sounds like "hat" in Korean.

661
00:24:41,928 --> 00:24:43,528
Mung bean sprouts? Should we add them?

662
00:24:43,958 --> 00:24:45,898
Yes. They wanted mung bean sprouts.

663
00:24:45,968 --> 00:24:47,868
Small napa cabbage, Chinese glass noodles.

664
00:24:48,198 --> 00:24:49,638
- How about tofu? - Tofu?

665
00:24:49,768 --> 00:24:51,097
Dried tofu.

666
00:24:51,098 --> 00:24:52,508
- Dried tofu? - Yes.

667
00:24:54,038 --> 00:24:55,507
Did you add Chinese glass noodles?

668
00:24:55,508 --> 00:24:57,077
"Chinese wide glass noodles?"

669
00:24:57,078 --> 00:24:58,578
(They're adding ingredients even though they're a bit slow.)

670
00:25:00,578 --> 00:25:03,448
Are wood ear and snow ear different?

671
00:25:04,918 --> 00:25:06,147
They wrote both.

672
00:25:06,148 --> 00:25:08,348
"Wood ear, snow ear."

673
00:25:11,658 --> 00:25:13,287
- It says "black wood ear." - What?

674
00:25:13,288 --> 00:25:14,927
- Black wood ear. - "Black wood ear?"

675
00:25:14,928 --> 00:25:17,057
- Should we add black wood ear? - What's that?

676
00:25:17,058 --> 00:25:18,327
Should we add both black wood ear and snow ear?

677
00:25:18,328 --> 00:25:20,797
(Adding black wood ear and snow ear)

678
00:25:20,798 --> 00:25:22,637
Why are there so many ingredients?

679
00:25:22,638 --> 00:25:24,198
- There's a lot. - Why?

680
00:25:24,998 --> 00:25:27,938
"A lot of zhi ma jiang?" Did they write anything about it?

681
00:25:29,208 --> 00:25:30,538
No.

682
00:25:31,308 --> 00:25:32,708
First off...

683
00:25:33,148 --> 00:25:34,578
What are "corn noodles?"

684
00:25:36,618 --> 00:25:39,887
(Should we go and ask them?)

685
00:25:39,888 --> 00:25:40,987
- Hand the phone to them. - What?

686
00:25:40,988 --> 00:25:42,188
Hand it to them.

687
00:25:43,458 --> 00:25:45,418
Guys, what do you want to do with the zhi ma jiang?

688
00:25:45,518 --> 00:25:46,787
- What? Zhi ma jiang? - Yes.

689
00:25:46,788 --> 00:25:47,987
Just the basics.

690
00:25:47,988 --> 00:25:48,988
- The basics? - Yes.

691
00:25:48,989 --> 00:25:50,727
- Pickled radish? - No, thanks.

692
00:25:50,728 --> 00:25:51,997
- No? - Jjyu.

693
00:25:51,998 --> 00:25:54,097
Can you check how we look?

694
00:25:54,098 --> 00:25:55,727
- You look great. - Well...

695
00:25:55,728 --> 00:25:57,767
You look the best.

696
00:25:57,768 --> 00:25:58,968
(Complimenting them without even looking at them)

697
00:25:59,838 --> 00:26:01,407
- Oh, right. Guo bao rou! - Guo bao rou?

698
00:26:01,408 --> 00:26:03,038
Please order guo bao rou.

699
00:26:03,708 --> 00:26:04,937
I did.

700
00:26:04,938 --> 00:26:08,348
(He orders guo bao rou for them.)

701
00:26:08,478 --> 00:26:09,678
Let's get it started.

702
00:26:12,218 --> 00:26:16,488
(The group shoot begins.)

703
00:26:16,588 --> 00:26:18,987
Nice. Liv, put your hands together. That looks pretty.

704
00:26:18,988 --> 00:26:19,988
Okay.

705
00:26:20,328 --> 00:26:22,727
Okay. Good.

706
00:26:22,728 --> 00:26:24,997
(Liv, May)

707
00:26:24,998 --> 00:26:26,097
Good job.

708
00:26:26,098 --> 00:26:27,197
A little more playfully.

709
00:26:27,198 --> 00:26:28,328
You can get closer.

710
00:26:28,668 --> 00:26:29,867
Playfully.

711
00:26:29,868 --> 00:26:31,338
(They're perfectly in sync, even without saying a word.)

712
00:26:31,938 --> 00:26:33,138
Nice.

713
00:26:33,468 --> 00:26:38,208
(RESCENE shines with the charm of all five members.)

714
00:26:38,808 --> 00:26:40,308
Nice.

715
00:26:40,808 --> 00:26:44,718
(They nail the photoshoot with ease, like the trending idols they are.)

716
00:26:44,778 --> 00:26:47,188
(They're all doing great.)

717
00:26:47,748 --> 00:26:48,848
(Exclaiming)

718
00:26:48,888 --> 00:26:51,058
It just skyrocketed overnight.

719
00:26:51,818 --> 00:26:55,828
This must feel like a dream right now.

720
00:26:56,428 --> 00:26:59,568
After performing at school fields and local community events,

721
00:27:00,028 --> 00:27:01,297
they suddenly...

722
00:27:01,298 --> 00:27:03,038
At KCON,

723
00:27:03,938 --> 00:27:06,938
it's mainly for international fans.

724
00:27:08,138 --> 00:27:11,737
(My Stars returned from performing at KCON LA.)

725
00:27:11,738 --> 00:27:13,008
It's held in LA.

726
00:27:13,208 --> 00:27:14,407
So many international fans...

727
00:27:14,408 --> 00:27:18,778
filled that huge hall.

728
00:27:19,218 --> 00:27:21,988
(International fans filled the venue.)

729
00:27:22,518 --> 00:27:24,187
Aren't they all overseas Koreans?

730
00:27:24,188 --> 00:27:25,357
- No. - No?

731
00:27:25,358 --> 00:27:26,427
Foreign people.

732
00:27:26,428 --> 00:27:27,758
Overseas Koreans don't come.

733
00:27:28,358 --> 00:27:30,328
- In the past, it was mostly... - Not these days.

734
00:27:30,528 --> 00:27:32,427
Is it "Gayo Stage?"

735
00:27:32,428 --> 00:27:34,097
I guess things have changed a lot.

736
00:27:34,098 --> 00:27:35,798
Overseas Koreans?

737
00:27:36,268 --> 00:27:37,868
Our overseas Koreans.

738
00:27:38,968 --> 00:27:40,508
I want a sip.

739
00:27:40,938 --> 00:27:42,237
- I'm thirsty. - Woni...

740
00:27:42,238 --> 00:27:43,538
No.

741
00:27:44,738 --> 00:27:45,837
Woni.

742
00:27:45,838 --> 00:27:47,178
Should we ask Jjyu-Kkyu?

743
00:27:47,848 --> 00:27:49,077
(Hesitating)

744
00:27:49,078 --> 00:27:51,547
(Glancing)

745
00:27:51,548 --> 00:27:56,918
(My Stars aren't comfortable with the senior secretaries.)

746
00:27:57,558 --> 00:27:59,787
I'm thirsty, Jjyu-Kkyu.

747
00:27:59,788 --> 00:28:00,857
(Gathering up her courage)

748
00:28:00,858 --> 00:28:02,758
I'm thirsty, Jjyu-Kkyu.

749
00:28:05,128 --> 00:28:06,398
Would you like a lemon-lime soda?

750
00:28:06,798 --> 00:28:07,868
Yes, please!

751
00:28:08,528 --> 00:28:09,767
- They want a lemon-lime soda. - What?

752
00:28:09,768 --> 00:28:10,837
They want a lemon-lime soda.

753
00:28:10,838 --> 00:28:13,208
(My Stars worked up the courage to ask for a lemon-lime soda.)

754
00:28:14,438 --> 00:28:18,038
(Even setting up a custom tray)

755
00:28:18,508 --> 00:28:19,808
Put them here.

756
00:28:21,148 --> 00:28:22,208
Even a tray?

757
00:28:23,018 --> 00:28:26,188
(Giggling over even the smallest acts of care)

758
00:28:26,318 --> 00:28:27,817
Jjyu is cute.

759
00:28:27,818 --> 00:28:29,518
He's cute.

760
00:28:29,918 --> 00:28:31,018
This is Woni's.

761
00:28:31,688 --> 00:28:32,888
Liv.

762
00:28:33,158 --> 00:28:34,288
Put the straws.

763
00:28:36,898 --> 00:28:38,828
(Floating)

764
00:28:39,828 --> 00:28:41,928
(Floating)

765
00:28:42,768 --> 00:28:46,438
(All the straws are floating.)

766
00:28:47,338 --> 00:28:50,107
(Taking care of all 5 slows things down.)

767
00:28:50,108 --> 00:28:51,378
Let's begin.

768
00:28:52,878 --> 00:28:54,308
You're late, Jjyu-Kkyu.

769
00:28:58,278 --> 00:29:00,418
I'm sorry.

770
00:29:01,188 --> 00:29:02,587
- We can't give it to them. - First...

771
00:29:02,588 --> 00:29:04,187
Let's have a test shot.

772
00:29:04,188 --> 00:29:06,228
(He waits in front of them.)

773
00:29:06,888 --> 00:29:07,957
Give me a moment.

774
00:29:07,958 --> 00:29:09,798
- Go in there now. - A moment, please.

775
00:29:10,498 --> 00:29:11,798
A moment, please.

776
00:29:12,158 --> 00:29:14,198
They'll just have a sip.

777
00:29:14,528 --> 00:29:16,737
- Straws too. Amazing. - Amazing.

778
00:29:16,738 --> 00:29:18,168
- Even straws. - They even did that?

779
00:29:18,238 --> 00:29:19,608
- Thank you. - You're the best.

780
00:29:19,668 --> 00:29:21,508
- What... - Kkyu.

781
00:29:21,908 --> 00:29:23,938
This is touching.

782
00:29:25,078 --> 00:29:27,048
This is a tip.

783
00:29:27,478 --> 00:29:30,217
(Using the can tab to hold the straw in place)

784
00:29:30,218 --> 00:29:31,348
Amazing.

785
00:29:32,278 --> 00:29:33,317
I'm Korean.

