00:38:31,688 --> 00:38:33,088
(Just give it to me first.)

1055
00:38:33,588 --> 00:38:34,727
(His lifelong dream comes true.)

1056
00:38:34,728 --> 00:38:36,257
- Okay. - Okay.

1057
00:38:36,258 --> 00:38:39,197
- That one is a bit big. - Okay.

1058
00:38:39,198 --> 00:38:40,698
(Happiness squeezing his finger)

1059
00:38:41,498 --> 00:38:43,638
(She gets ready to eat after taking off her rings.)

1060
00:38:44,338 --> 00:38:46,267
(Getting some noodles)

1061
00:38:46,268 --> 00:38:47,767
How could you go to LA...

1062
00:38:47,768 --> 00:38:49,267
when you're not popular?

1063
00:38:49,268 --> 00:38:51,277
- I haven't been to LA in my life. - You went to KCON.

1064
00:38:51,278 --> 00:38:52,278
That means you're famous.

1065
00:38:52,279 --> 00:38:54,477
(Taking a sip of the broth too)

1066
00:38:54,478 --> 00:38:56,517
(Getting a spoonful of rice)

1067
00:38:56,518 --> 00:38:58,378
She's eating well.

1068
00:38:58,648 --> 00:39:00,018
Do we have water?

1069
00:39:02,318 --> 00:39:03,488
This is so good.

1070
00:39:03,818 --> 00:39:05,158
So good.

1071
00:39:07,288 --> 00:39:08,587
I think Korean food is the best.

1072
00:39:08,588 --> 00:39:09,628
(I'm suited for Korean food.)

1073
00:39:09,898 --> 00:39:11,127
(Is she really Japanese?)

1074
00:39:11,128 --> 00:39:12,128
Right?

1075
00:39:13,498 --> 00:39:15,997
Woni, please get changed.

1076
00:39:15,998 --> 00:39:17,868
(Being summoned for the 2nd time)

1077
00:39:18,038 --> 00:39:19,398
I think they're calling me.

1078
00:39:20,068 --> 00:39:21,537
Go slowly.

1079
00:39:21,538 --> 00:39:22,808
She'll get there in five minutes.

1080
00:39:24,508 --> 00:39:26,608
- Keep eating. - Can you do that?

1081
00:39:26,648 --> 00:39:27,947
Just eat.

1082
00:39:27,948 --> 00:39:29,678
(Genie will protect My Star's mealtime.)

1083
00:39:29,878 --> 00:39:32,747
(Glancing)

1084
00:39:32,748 --> 00:39:34,218
It's okay. Don't be worried.

1085
00:39:35,248 --> 00:39:37,187
You're popular now. Don't worry.

1086
00:39:37,188 --> 00:39:38,757
(Joking)

1087
00:39:38,758 --> 00:39:40,658
You're popular now. Don't worry.

1088
00:39:43,528 --> 00:39:44,697
(Worried look)

1089
00:39:44,698 --> 00:39:46,458
You're popular now. Why are you so worried?

1090
00:39:47,098 --> 00:39:48,968
- I guess we're popular. - You are.

1091
00:39:49,368 --> 00:39:51,637
How long has it been? A year?

1092
00:39:51,638 --> 00:39:52,938
- No. - We're not popular.

1093
00:39:53,068 --> 00:39:54,607
- We're not popular. - You are popular.

1094
00:39:54,608 --> 00:39:56,207
You're popular now.

1095
00:39:56,208 --> 00:39:57,877
- How could you go to LA... - You can do this much.

1096
00:39:57,878 --> 00:39:59,208
when you're not popular?

1097
00:39:59,408 --> 00:40:01,847
We're filming with Jjyu-Kkyu.

1098
00:40:01,848 --> 00:40:03,147
- We're popular. - Right.

1099
00:40:03,148 --> 00:40:04,677
- This situation itself... - Right.

1100
00:40:04,678 --> 00:40:06,048
(Are we popular?)

1101
00:40:06,448 --> 00:40:07,588
Whatever.

1102
00:40:08,718 --> 00:40:09,917
Did you eat enough?

1103
00:40:09,918 --> 00:40:11,957
We're not suddenly going to get paid less, right?

1104
00:40:11,958 --> 00:40:13,057
That won't happen.

1105
00:40:13,058 --> 00:40:14,087
You have to raise your rate for the next one...

1106
00:40:14,088 --> 00:40:15,158
since you're popular.

1107
00:40:16,628 --> 00:40:18,398
Don't make it too easy for them.

1108
00:40:19,528 --> 00:40:21,698
(Worried look)

1109
00:40:23,028 --> 00:40:24,998
I don't know what to say.

1110
00:40:27,608 --> 00:40:28,638
Jjyu?

1111
00:40:29,208 --> 00:40:32,008
Everything he said...

1112
00:40:32,638 --> 00:40:34,377
were pieces of advice...

1113
00:40:34,378 --> 00:40:37,578
that we couldn't get from the adults around us.

1114
00:40:38,078 --> 00:40:39,818
They have to enjoy things...

1115
00:40:40,088 --> 00:40:41,888
when they're doing well.

1116
00:40:42,888 --> 00:40:44,458
It would be nice if they keep doing well,

1117
00:40:45,258 --> 00:40:47,528
and if they don't, they can think about the good old days.

1118
00:40:47,588 --> 00:40:49,928
They'll live quietly like that.

1119
00:40:50,558 --> 00:40:52,597
What else can they do? That's how life is.

1120
00:40:52,598 --> 00:40:53,668
(Seo Jin's rational advice that threatens their innocence)

1121
00:40:54,498 --> 00:40:57,737
(Woni heads to get ready for her individual shoot.)

1122
00:40:57,738 --> 00:40:59,437
- Your slippers. - I don't need them.

1123
00:40:59,438 --> 00:41:01,338
- Is that all right? - Thank you.

1124
00:41:01,468 --> 00:41:04,008
(Running barefoot)

1125
00:41:04,938 --> 00:41:07,848
My stomach is about to burst.

1126
00:41:08,308 --> 00:41:11,318
(May and Zena head to get ready for their shoot.)

1127
00:41:12,148 --> 00:41:13,448
Chew it well.

1128
00:41:13,618 --> 00:41:15,547
I eat really well.

1129
00:41:15,548 --> 00:41:16,918
Of course.

1130
00:41:17,288 --> 00:41:19,658
You're good at using the chopsticks even though you're a foreigner.

1131
00:41:20,588 --> 00:41:23,228
(Of course, she is. She's Japanese.)

1132
00:41:23,928 --> 00:41:25,198
You can speak in Japanese.

1133
00:41:26,868 --> 00:41:28,568
- Would that be okay? - Yes!

1134
00:41:29,698 --> 00:41:31,038
Mr. Manager?

1135
00:41:31,468 --> 00:41:32,698
Mr. Manager?

1136
00:41:33,768 --> 00:41:34,768
What?

1137
00:41:35,938 --> 00:41:37,437
- That was really... - That was...

1138
00:41:37,438 --> 00:41:39,708
That was English.

1139
00:41:40,308 --> 00:41:41,877
He couldn't understand because it was English.

1140
00:41:41,878 --> 00:41:42,977
She said, "Mr. Manager."

1141
00:41:42,978 --> 00:41:44,317
Did you say, "Mr. Manager?"

1142
00:41:44,318 --> 00:41:47,317
I was so nervous. I couldn't hear that.

1143
00:41:47,318 --> 00:41:48,347
(I couldn't hear it because I was nervous.)

1144
00:41:48,348 --> 00:41:50,518
I'm sorry.

1145
00:41:50,988 --> 00:41:52,158
This is so funny.

1146
00:41:53,388 --> 00:41:55,528
Japanese restaurants...

1147
00:41:55,688 --> 00:41:58,098
Why do they charge extra for kimchi?

1148
00:41:59,328 --> 00:42:01,297
(He just speaks in 0 languages now.)

1149
00:42:01,298 --> 00:42:02,827
- I'm curious. - He just...

1150
00:42:02,828 --> 00:42:05,338
He mostly spoke in Korean.

1151
00:42:06,198 --> 00:42:08,268
No, no.

1152
00:42:09,238 --> 00:42:11,007
The reason for that...

1153
00:42:11,008 --> 00:42:12,038
Yes.

1154
00:42:12,808 --> 00:42:14,348
He already doesn't understand.

1155
00:42:15,378 --> 00:42:16,777
(The reason for that...)

1156
00:42:16,778 --> 00:42:18,178
(That was too difficult for Kwang Kyu.)

1157
00:42:18,248 --> 00:42:19,448
How many times have you been to Japan?

1158
00:42:20,088 --> 00:42:21,218
Japan...

1159
00:42:21,888 --> 00:42:23,388
I went there once with you.

1160
00:42:24,558 --> 00:42:27,488
For Seo Jin's fan signing event.

1161
00:42:28,158 --> 00:42:30,428
- It was a fan meeting. - Fan meeting?

1162
00:42:31,358 --> 00:42:34,367
The venue was filled with people.

1163
00:42:34,368 --> 00:42:37,138
- Amazing. - It was really...

1164
00:42:38,698 --> 00:42:40,368
That's amazing.

1165
00:42:40,738 --> 00:42:43,168
There would have been so many people.

1166
00:42:43,708 --> 00:42:45,238
Besides Tokyo, where else have you been?

1167
00:42:46,338 --> 00:42:47,648
I've been everywhere.

1168
00:42:48,578 --> 00:42:49,877
- Really? - Yes.

1169
00:42:49,878 --> 00:42:50,878
(Laughing)

1170
00:42:50,978 --> 00:42:54,087
He had many girlfriends.

1171
00:42:54,088 --> 00:42:55,888
- He had many girlfriends. - Yes.

1172
00:42:56,048 --> 00:42:58,318
He had many girlfriends long time ago.

1173
00:42:58,518 --> 00:43:00,288
He had many girlfriends.

1174
00:43:03,258 --> 00:43:05,198
You could have stayed in Japan.

1175
00:43:05,628 --> 00:43:08,797
Why did you want to become an idol in Korea?

1176
00:43:08,798 --> 00:43:10,668
You could have debuted in Japan.

1177
00:43:11,538 --> 00:43:13,708
I wanted to be...

1178
00:43:14,308 --> 00:43:15,767
a global artist...

1179
00:43:15,768 --> 00:43:20,007
who is known by the whole world and even go to the US.

1180
00:43:20,008 --> 00:43:21,208
- Ever since you were young? - Yes.

1181
00:43:21,908 --> 00:43:25,318
I saw Korean artists...

1182
00:43:25,578 --> 00:43:28,618
win Billboard awards in the US...

1183
00:43:29,148 --> 00:43:32,388
and realized that the Korean market was really big.

1184
00:43:32,618 --> 00:43:36,728
I thought I would have a better chance to succeed.

1185
00:43:37,798 --> 00:43:39,198
So that's why you're studying English hard.

1186
00:43:39,428 --> 00:43:41,027
Right. I'm studying English.

1187
00:43:41,028 --> 00:43:43,168
Being fluent in English would be a plus.

1188
00:43:43,538 --> 00:43:45,798
I also have a sense of patriotism...

1189
00:43:46,068 --> 00:43:47,968
toward Japan.

1190
00:43:48,068 --> 00:43:50,708
I was proud...

1191
00:43:51,308 --> 00:43:53,238
to be Japanese.

1192
00:43:54,348 --> 00:43:57,678
But when I came to Korea, the trainees here...

1193
00:43:58,418 --> 00:44:00,318
- were very talented. - No, I'm fine.

1194
00:44:00,818 --> 00:44:02,347
They practiced so much.

1195
00:44:02,348 --> 00:44:04,918
The culture itself was different,

1196
00:44:05,318 --> 00:44:08,428
so I was shocked by that.

1197
00:44:09,688 --> 00:44:12,497
(She worked even harder to keep up with the competition.)

1198
00:44:12,498 --> 00:44:15,328
I wanted to reach...

1199
00:44:15,498 --> 00:44:16,998
a bigger world.

1200
00:44:17,898 --> 00:44:20,207
I decided to achieve that.

1201
00:44:20,208 --> 00:44:22,667
(Pursuing her dream of becoming a global artist in Korea)

1202
00:44:22,668 --> 00:44:24,107
(My Stars' schedule:)

1203
00:44:24,108 --> 00:44:25,337
(Time: 3pm, Location: Outdoor studio,)

1204
00:44:25,338 --> 00:44:26,378
(Details: Group ad shoot)

1205
00:44:26,578 --> 00:44:29,548
(Rain pours before the outdoor shoot.)

1206
00:44:29,878 --> 00:44:35,248
(Everyone is busy because of the sudden rain.)

1207
00:44:35,748 --> 00:44:37,217
It's raining a lot.

1208
00:44:37,218 --> 00:44:38,817
- It's a relief this was set up. - This...

1209
00:44:38,818 --> 00:44:40,228
(She's worried.)

1210
00:44:40,458 --> 00:44:43,428
(They wait under a tent until the rain stops.)

1211
00:44:43,928 --> 00:44:45,757
- Wait a minute. - What are you doing?

1212
00:44:45,758 --> 00:44:47,797
It's raining, and Kkyu and Jjyu are gone.

1213
00:44:47,798 --> 00:44:49,628
- We're waiting outside, - Right.

1214
00:44:49,768 --> 00:44:52,197
while Kkyu and Jjyu are inside. Is this okay?

1215
00:44:52,198 --> 00:44:53,537
They're...

1216
00:44:53,538 --> 00:44:54,637
(My Stars rapidly fire off their complaints.)

1217
00:44:54,638 --> 00:44:56,238
Are they sitting inside?

1218
00:44:57,808 --> 00:44:58,938
We're out here.

1219
00:45:01,208 --> 00:45:02,647
Their ears would probably itch...

1220
00:45:02,648 --> 00:45:04,147
because we're talking about them.

1221
00:45:04,148 --> 00:45:05,178
Right.

1222
00:45:05,878 --> 00:45:08,418
(Meanwhile, Kkyu, whose ears would be itching...)

1223
00:45:09,388 --> 00:45:11,587
Hold on.

1224
00:45:11,588 --> 00:45:12,688
(He's escorting Minami out after she got changed.)

1225
00:45:13,218 --> 00:45:14,258
My shoes!

1226
00:45:14,388 --> 00:45:16,187
Are these yours? Really?

1227
00:45:16,188 --> 00:45:17,427
- Wait. - It's okay.

1228
00:45:17,428 --> 00:45:18,428
Is it okay?

1229
00:45:18,429 --> 00:45:21,068
(He wore her shoes with the heels folded down.)

1230
00:45:22,528 --> 00:45:24,167
Slowly.

1231
00:45:24,168 --> 00:45:26,937
(He takes care of Minami with an umbrella.)

1232
00:45:26,938 --> 00:45:30,138
- Okay. Go! - Go!

1233
00:45:30,708 --> 00:45:31,778
(Rushing)

1234
00:45:32,478 --> 00:45:34,908
Thank you!

1235
00:45:35,178 --> 00:45:37,918
(My Star's scalp is precious.)

1236
00:45:38,478 --> 00:45:41,218
Kkyu. You can move to the rhythm.

1237
00:45:42,148 --> 00:45:43,388
I'm an expert at rhythms.

1238
00:45:44,688 --> 00:45:46,218
If it's what My Stars want,

1239
00:45:46,558 --> 00:45:48,227
I can do anything.

1240
00:45:48,228 --> 00:45:52,198
(Secretary Kkyu keeps their spirits up during the wait.)

1241
00:45:52,428 --> 00:45:54,698
Hold on. What's Jjyu doing when you're here?

1242
00:45:54,768 --> 00:45:56,567
- What's Jjyu doing? - You're out here in the rain.

1243
00:45:56,568 --> 00:45:58,267
He just came out.

1244
00:45:58,268 --> 00:45:59,368
- Jjyu! - Jjyu!

1245
00:45:59,838 --> 00:46:00,908
- Jjyu! - Jjyu!

1246
00:46:01,638 --> 00:46:04,378
(He's caught trying to slack off.)

1247
00:46:04,808 --> 00:46:07,007
(Chirping and calling for Jjyu in one voice)

1248
00:46:07,008 --> 00:46:09,177
- Jjyu! - Jjyu! Hurry up!

1249
00:46:09,178 --> 00:46:10,248
(Come out quickly.)

1250
00:46:10,718 --> 00:46:12,448
I think Jjyu is a bit slow.

1251
00:46:12,848 --> 00:46:14,548
(Gasping)

1252
00:46:14,988 --> 00:46:16,347
(Exclaiming)

1253
00:46:16,348 --> 00:46:17,588
"Isn't he going to come?"

1254
00:46:19,618 --> 00:46:20,757
(Glancing)

1255
00:46:20,758 --> 00:46:23,028
(I'm sorry.)

1256
00:46:25,258 --> 00:46:27,868
- I think he's still... - There he is.

1257
00:46:28,668 --> 00:46:31,738
(Jjyu comes out with an umbrella.)

1258
00:46:32,038 --> 00:46:33,638
Jjyu, you're so slow.

1259
00:46:33,808 --> 00:46:35,137
- Ready? - Yes.

1260
00:46:35,138 --> 00:46:36,507
Come inside the tent.

1261
00:46:36,508 --> 00:46:38,008
(It's raining.)

1262
00:46:38,238 --> 00:46:41,247
(They wait for the rain to stop.)

1263
00:46:41,248 --> 00:46:42,348
Hey.

1264
00:46:42,508 --> 00:46:43,577
Don't you feel it?

1265
00:46:43,578 --> 00:46:44,947
(There are also mosquitoes.)

1266
00:46:44,948 --> 00:46:47,088
I think I got a mosquito bite.

1267
00:46:47,388 --> 00:46:48,547
Did you spray mosquito repellent?

1268
00:46:48,548 --> 00:46:50,047
- No. - Do you want it?

1269
00:46:50,048 --> 00:46:51,118
Yes, please.

1270
00:46:51,918 --> 00:46:53,728
Kwang Kyu, can you get me the mosquito spray?

1271
00:46:54,888 --> 00:47:00,498
(Here comes the mosquito repellent.)

1272
00:47:01,728 --> 00:47:04,967
(Because we can't let precious My Stars get bitten by mosquitoes)

1273
00:47:04,968 --> 00:47:06,398
- Me too. - Me too.

1274
00:47:09,008 --> 00:47:11,308
(Holding his breath to spray)

1275
00:47:11,908 --> 00:47:14,707
(Kyu the pest control only for My Stars)

1276
00:47:14,708 --> 00:47:15,748
(Exhaling)

1277
00:47:16,608 --> 00:47:18,748
I was holding my breath. I'm dizzy now.

1278
00:47:19,648 --> 00:47:21,047
Do you want us to spray it on you?

1279
00:47:21,048 --> 00:47:22,848
- What? - Do you want us to spray it on you?

1280
00:47:23,488 --> 00:47:24,758
Raise your arms and turn around.

1281
00:47:25,018 --> 00:47:26,317
Turn around.

1282
00:47:26,318 --> 00:47:28,158
Hey, don't do it on his face.

1283
00:47:28,428 --> 00:47:30,287
(Spraying the mosquito repellent on his face by accident)

1284
00:47:30,288 --> 00:47:31,458
Only on his body.

1285
00:47:31,998 --> 00:47:34,597
Hey, you just sprayed it on his face.

1286
00:47:34,598 --> 00:47:35,798
I'm sorry.

1287
00:47:36,768 --> 00:47:39,437
- You sprayed it right on my face. - I'm sorry.

1288
00:47:39,438 --> 00:47:40,508
Tomorrow...

1289
00:47:41,038 --> 00:47:42,137
I don't need it.

1290
00:47:42,138 --> 00:47:43,567
- Still. - I don't need it.

1291
00:47:43,568 --> 00:47:45,177
- We'll do it for you. - No.

1292
00:47:45,178 --> 00:47:46,308
The rain stopped.

1293
00:47:47,378 --> 00:47:48,378
Get ready for the group photo.

1294
00:47:48,379 --> 00:47:50,207
Get ready for the group photo.

1295
00:47:50,208 --> 00:47:51,278
- Okay. - Okay.

1296
00:47:51,448 --> 00:47:52,678
Wait.

1297
00:47:53,248 --> 00:47:54,347
This way?

1298
00:47:54,348 --> 00:47:56,787
- Oh, thank you. - Thank you.

1299
00:47:56,788 --> 00:47:58,087
Thank you so much.

1300
00:47:58,088 --> 00:47:59,117
(Spraying the mosquito repellent to the end)

1301
00:47:59,118 --> 00:48:00,358
Wait. Did you spray it again?

1302
00:48:01,928 --> 00:48:04,158
Pretend you're playing.

1303
00:48:04,828 --> 00:48:05,857
Go.

1304
00:48:05,858 --> 00:48:06,858
(Pretending to have fun)

1305
00:48:06,859 --> 00:48:09,067
Okay. Good.

1306
00:48:09,068 --> 00:48:10,537
Keep smiling.

1307
00:48:10,538 --> 00:48:12,968
Keep smiling. Look cheerful.

1308
00:48:13,268 --> 00:48:14,308
That's good.

1309
00:48:14,938 --> 00:48:16,608
Enjoy it while it lasts.

1310
00:48:17,008 --> 00:48:18,778
They're happy because they became famous.

1311
00:48:19,908 --> 00:48:21,108
They couldn't be happier.

1312
00:48:21,708 --> 00:48:22,878
Okay.

1313
00:48:24,448 --> 00:48:27,048
Smile.

1314
00:48:27,388 --> 00:48:28,388
That's good.

1315
00:48:28,389 --> 00:48:29,888
- That's good. - Jjyu and Kkyu, make us smile.

1316
00:48:30,048 --> 00:48:31,817
- Try to look cheerful. - Make us laugh.

1317
00:48:31,818 --> 00:48:34,228
You can face each other.

1318
00:48:34,528 --> 00:48:35,857
