00:57:41,738 --> 00:57:43,808
- Go, RESCENE. - Thank you.

1586
00:57:44,478 --> 00:57:45,938
Yaho!

1587
00:57:46,278 --> 00:57:49,608
(May has a good idea.)

1588
00:57:50,078 --> 00:57:53,847
(Please make RESCENE more successful.)

1589
00:57:53,848 --> 00:57:55,617
Like building a stone tower.

1590
00:57:55,618 --> 00:57:56,818
Right.

1591
00:57:57,348 --> 00:57:58,587
I see.

1592
00:57:58,588 --> 00:58:00,757
- Gimbap. - Right?

1593
00:58:00,758 --> 00:58:02,058
(He'll even become a stone tower for My Stars.)

1594
00:58:02,588 --> 00:58:04,157
I should've done it with the girls.

1595
00:58:04,158 --> 00:58:06,627
(Woni joins the wax squishies.)

1596
00:58:06,628 --> 00:58:09,468
I saw it on the news...

1597
00:58:09,568 --> 00:58:12,838
that it's too toxic for children.

1598
00:58:12,968 --> 00:58:16,707
I heard the ones with the KFC mark are okay.

1599
00:58:16,708 --> 00:58:17,837
KFC?

1600
00:58:17,838 --> 00:58:19,077
- KFC is... - That's a fried chicken place.

1601
00:58:19,078 --> 00:58:21,107
Isn't that KS?

1602
00:58:21,108 --> 00:58:23,078
(Even worse)

1603
00:58:23,548 --> 00:58:24,717
"KFC..."

1604
00:58:24,718 --> 00:58:25,878
(You mean the KC mark?)

1605
00:58:25,918 --> 00:58:27,748
KF?

1606
00:58:27,788 --> 00:58:28,788
- K... - KFC?

1607
00:58:28,789 --> 00:58:30,147
You don't know.

1608
00:58:30,148 --> 00:58:32,357
KC. It's okay if it has the KC mark on it.

1609
00:58:32,358 --> 00:58:33,988
(She remembered.)

1610
00:58:35,358 --> 00:58:37,128
It's okay if it has the KC mark on it.

1611
00:58:37,228 --> 00:58:38,957
Don't air that, please.

1612
00:58:38,958 --> 00:58:40,357
- It's embarrassing. - Cut.

1613
00:58:40,358 --> 00:58:43,368
- Anything with the KC mark is fine. - You know what to do.

1614
00:58:43,468 --> 00:58:45,668
You even know how editing works.

1615
00:58:45,938 --> 00:58:47,168
How much is this?

1616
00:58:47,938 --> 00:58:49,907
It's expensive these days. Over ten dollars.

1617
00:58:49,908 --> 00:58:50,908
- For one? - Yes.

1618
00:58:50,909 --> 00:58:52,337
The one you just popped.

1619
00:58:52,338 --> 00:58:53,908
You'd pay over ten dollars for this?

1620
00:58:54,008 --> 00:58:56,478
We just lost one fried chicken.

1621
00:58:56,578 --> 00:58:57,978
It really is KFC.

1622
00:58:58,878 --> 00:59:01,087
(Failing to change the subject)

1623
00:59:01,088 --> 00:59:03,688
- Right? - Stop saying that.

1624
00:59:04,558 --> 00:59:06,157
Jjyu! Kkyu!

1625
00:59:06,158 --> 00:59:08,287
Why do you keep embarrassing your artist?

1626
00:59:08,288 --> 00:59:10,327
- You can't do that. - Seriously.

1627
00:59:10,328 --> 00:59:11,798
(Let me protect my youngest!)

1628
00:59:11,898 --> 00:59:13,328
Protect your artist.

1629
00:59:13,358 --> 00:59:16,397
- Artist... - Protect the artist?

1630
00:59:16,398 --> 00:59:18,498
We can't do that to our artists.

1631
00:59:18,868 --> 00:59:20,967
Have you got paid?

1632
00:59:20,968 --> 00:59:23,207
- No, not yet. - No?

1633
00:59:23,208 --> 00:59:25,577
So you need to...

1634
00:59:25,578 --> 00:59:28,107
save up.

1635
00:59:28,108 --> 00:59:30,377
If you invest in weird places...

1636
00:59:30,378 --> 00:59:31,948
and they go wrong,

1637
00:59:32,078 --> 00:59:33,417
you lose everything.

1638
00:59:33,418 --> 00:59:35,217
But we don't know...

1639
00:59:35,218 --> 00:59:36,517
anything about stocks.

1640
00:59:36,518 --> 00:59:37,987
You don't need to know that.

1641
00:59:37,988 --> 00:59:39,488
When you get paid later,

1642
00:59:40,088 --> 00:59:42,528
don't waste it.

1643
00:59:42,628 --> 00:59:43,927
Be frugal and save your money.

1644
00:59:43,928 --> 00:59:46,127
- Don't look for a jackpot... - I'm going to buy squishies.

1645
00:59:46,128 --> 00:59:47,327
- We can buy squishies. - Don't buy...

1646
00:59:47,328 --> 00:59:49,497
more than 3 or 4. Do you hear me?

1647
00:59:49,498 --> 00:59:51,467
Don't buy a dozen like this.

1648
00:59:51,468 --> 00:59:52,668
- Okay. - Do you hear me?

1649
00:59:53,138 --> 00:59:54,197
- We already bought a dozen. - Don't spend your money on weird...

1650
00:59:54,198 --> 00:59:56,608
Then what do you do for fun?

1651
00:59:57,268 --> 00:59:58,337
Me?

1652
00:59:58,338 --> 01:00:00,578
- Making fun of Kkyu. - Your small but definite happiness.

1653
01:00:00,778 --> 01:00:01,907
What's that?

1654
01:00:01,908 --> 01:00:03,007
(What's the small but definite happiness?)

1655
01:00:03,008 --> 01:00:05,018
Something that's small but definitely makes you happy.

1656
01:00:05,678 --> 01:00:07,478
First of all,

1657
01:00:07,988 --> 01:00:09,718
happiness depends on your attitude.

1658
01:00:10,388 --> 01:00:12,487
But if you make a lot of money, happiness automatically follows.

1659
01:00:12,488 --> 01:00:14,757
(But if you make a lot of money, happiness automatically follows.)

1660
01:00:14,758 --> 01:00:16,187
(Flustered)

1661
01:00:16,188 --> 01:00:18,328
It's guaranteed. You'll be happy.

1662
01:00:18,828 --> 01:00:20,427
- If you make money. - But is money really everything?

1663
01:00:20,428 --> 01:00:21,597
- I think... - It's everything.

1664
01:00:21,598 --> 01:00:22,767
It's everything.

1665
01:00:22,768 --> 01:00:23,967
- I think... - It's everything.

1666
01:00:23,968 --> 01:00:25,037
It's everything.

1667
01:00:25,038 --> 01:00:27,137
I don't know yet because I haven't made any yet.

1668
01:00:27,138 --> 01:00:28,208
It's everything.

1669
01:00:28,838 --> 01:00:29,908
It's everything.

1670
01:00:30,138 --> 01:00:32,877
(What a lesson.)

1671
01:00:32,878 --> 01:00:34,747
I think Jjyu is right.

1672
01:00:34,748 --> 01:00:36,707
The squishies don't make him happy,

1673
01:00:36,708 --> 01:00:38,078
but he always looks happy.

1674
01:00:38,148 --> 01:00:40,817
- Is that because he's rich? - He's...

1675
01:00:40,818 --> 01:00:44,557
He doesn't need to find happiness with minor stuff like this.

1676
01:00:44,558 --> 01:00:45,658
You got it.

1677
01:00:46,618 --> 01:00:49,028
I was shocked because...

1678
01:00:49,658 --> 01:00:51,757
I thought I didn't need money...

1679
01:00:51,758 --> 01:00:54,358
to be happy.

1680
01:00:55,628 --> 01:00:57,098
Anyway, is that true?

1681
01:00:57,168 --> 01:00:58,397
Somebody needs to tell me.

1682
01:00:58,398 --> 01:00:59,538
It might not be true.

1683
01:00:59,738 --> 01:01:03,837
Were you happy when you moved to a bigger house?

1684
01:01:03,838 --> 01:01:05,077
- I was so happy. - Hey.

1685
01:01:05,078 --> 01:01:06,578
- Oh, right there. - See?

1686
01:01:07,438 --> 01:01:08,878
- My goodness. - I get it now.

1687
01:01:08,948 --> 01:01:10,047
- What? - This is crazy.

1688
01:01:10,048 --> 01:01:11,877
It was already part of your life.

1689
01:01:11,878 --> 01:01:13,747
You just didn't realize it.

1690
01:01:13,748 --> 01:01:15,347
(Capitalism is already permeating.)

1691
01:01:15,348 --> 01:01:17,187
You're on the right track.

1692
01:01:17,188 --> 01:01:18,858
- I was already enjoying it. - Of course.

1693
01:01:19,818 --> 01:01:21,987
You're becoming the slave of capitalism.

1694
01:01:21,988 --> 01:01:23,458
(She has never met any grown-up like him before.)

1695
01:01:24,958 --> 01:01:28,868
(How's the shoot going?)

1696
01:01:29,828 --> 01:01:31,438
Oh, what is this?

1697
01:01:32,198 --> 01:01:33,838
What's here? It's catering.

1698
01:01:35,708 --> 01:01:37,608
- Did they call a buffet? - What?

1699
01:01:38,038 --> 01:01:39,277
Did they call a buffet?

1700
01:01:39,278 --> 01:01:40,407
(Food prepared by the production team)

1701
01:01:40,408 --> 01:01:41,648
A buffet...

1702
01:01:42,208 --> 01:01:43,748
We've already had that.

1703
01:01:45,078 --> 01:01:46,418
Oh, my gosh.

1704
01:01:46,978 --> 01:01:48,048
Woni.

1705
01:01:48,418 --> 01:01:49,887
- Do you want something to eat? - I'm here because I'm hungry.

1706
01:01:49,888 --> 01:01:51,557
You're hungry? But you ate so much.

1707
01:01:51,558 --> 01:01:52,718
- You're hungry again? - Yes.

1708
01:01:53,118 --> 01:01:54,257
Get whatever you need.

1709
01:01:54,258 --> 01:01:56,387
(Grabbing zucchini jeon)

1710
01:01:56,388 --> 01:01:58,158
- That's a vegetable. - Only zucchini jeon?

1711
01:01:59,128 --> 01:02:02,068
(Staring)

1712
01:02:02,628 --> 01:02:04,227
They're shooting.

1713
01:02:04,228 --> 01:02:05,697
They have to shoot, right?

1714
01:02:05,698 --> 01:02:07,698
Is that how you use chopsticks?

1715
01:02:08,338 --> 01:02:10,237
Is that how you use chopsticks?

1716
01:02:10,238 --> 01:02:11,337
(A strange way of using chopsticks)

1717
01:02:11,338 --> 01:02:12,477
You...

1718
01:02:12,478 --> 01:02:14,478
The way you use chopsticks...

1719
01:02:14,808 --> 01:02:16,747
I carry training chopsticks with me.

1720
01:02:16,748 --> 01:02:18,247
- For kids? - Yes.

1721
01:02:18,248 --> 01:02:20,648
- I'll do it. That's frustrating. - Yes. Do it for her.

1722
01:02:20,948 --> 01:02:22,588
Only meat? No vegetables?

1723
01:02:23,318 --> 01:02:24,518
- No vegetables. - What?

1724
01:02:24,888 --> 01:02:26,458
That's fine.

1725
01:02:27,258 --> 01:02:29,058
I get criticized a lot because of the way I use chopsticks.

1726
01:02:29,928 --> 01:02:31,028
Then you should learn.

1727
01:02:31,188 --> 01:02:32,798
- I'm practicing. - Yes.

1728
01:02:33,358 --> 01:02:34,797
You can practice while eating.

1729
01:02:34,798 --> 01:02:36,227
- Yes. Let's go. - Yes.

1730
01:02:36,228 --> 01:02:37,328
(He'll also teach her how to use chopsticks.)

1731
01:02:37,628 --> 01:02:40,368
(Preparing food for My Star first)

1732
01:02:41,198 --> 01:02:42,538
May, do you want some food too?

1733
01:02:42,938 --> 01:02:44,038
No, I'm good.

1734
01:02:44,438 --> 01:02:45,708
Eat a lot and make a lot.

1735
01:02:46,078 --> 01:02:48,177
How come you're not doing anything?

1736
01:02:48,178 --> 01:02:49,748
I'm going last.

1737
01:02:50,478 --> 01:02:53,518
(Trying to focus on the chopsticks)

1738
01:02:53,948 --> 01:02:56,388
(Watching carefully)

1739
01:02:58,118 --> 01:02:59,317
What are you doing?

1740
01:02:59,318 --> 01:03:00,388
(What are you doing?)

1741
01:03:00,858 --> 01:03:03,058
(Dangling)

1742
01:03:03,158 --> 01:03:04,287
What are you doing?

1743
01:03:04,288 --> 01:03:06,457
(The strangest way of using chopsticks)

1744
01:03:06,458 --> 01:03:08,297
Hey, you have to lean that on this finger.

1745
01:03:08,298 --> 01:03:09,728
(Lean the chopstick on the fourth finger.)

1746
01:03:10,128 --> 01:03:12,237
I think I got it, right?

1747
01:03:12,238 --> 01:03:13,937
- Yes, you got it. - Yes.

1748
01:03:13,938 --> 01:03:15,238
But I can't move them.

1749
01:03:15,908 --> 01:03:18,137
You need to practice that.

1750
01:03:18,138 --> 01:03:20,177
- How am I supposed to know? - Here.

1751
01:03:20,178 --> 01:03:21,607
Hold this.

1752
01:03:21,608 --> 01:03:23,648
Just move this.

1753
01:03:23,908 --> 01:03:25,417
- Does this stay still? - You should...

1754
01:03:25,418 --> 01:03:27,717
The fourth finger stays still.

1755
01:03:27,718 --> 01:03:28,848
(Keep the fourth finger still.)

1756
01:03:28,918 --> 01:03:30,887
Move this.

1757
01:03:30,888 --> 01:03:31,918
Do you see it?

1758
01:03:33,288 --> 01:03:34,757
- Okay. - Got it?

1759
01:03:34,758 --> 01:03:36,358
I think I got it.

1760
01:03:37,058 --> 01:03:39,628
(Leaning it on the fourth finger as she's taught)

1761
01:03:39,998 --> 01:03:41,397
(Staring)

1762
01:03:41,398 --> 01:03:43,468
No. I said you should lean it on the fourth finger.

1763
01:03:44,328 --> 01:03:45,637
(The chopstick man is impatient.)

1764
01:03:45,638 --> 01:03:47,297
Where on the fourth finger?

1765
01:03:47,298 --> 01:03:49,208
Lean it on the fourth finger. Is it leaning?

1766
01:03:49,268 --> 01:03:50,708
Yes, good. Lean that here.

1767
01:03:51,068 --> 01:03:52,278
- Try this. - Is this right?

1768
01:03:52,478 --> 01:03:53,978
- Yes. Here. - Yes.

1769
01:03:55,108 --> 01:03:56,447
Move this.

1770
01:03:56,448 --> 01:03:57,908
(He sounds quite kinder than you think.)

1771
01:03:58,318 --> 01:03:59,947
(What's the result of his strict training?)

1772
01:03:59,948 --> 01:04:01,418
Oh, you got it.

1773
01:04:01,618 --> 01:04:03,087
You got it. Good job.

1774
01:04:03,088 --> 01:04:05,188
You're a genius.

1775
01:04:05,258 --> 01:04:06,387
- Yes. - Good job.

1776
01:04:06,388 --> 01:04:07,457
You got it.

1777
01:04:07,458 --> 01:04:09,488
- Do you know how it works now? - You got it.

1778
01:04:10,458 --> 01:04:15,998
(Now she just needs to eat.)

1779
01:04:20,638 --> 01:04:22,468
(Eating smoothly)

1780
01:04:22,538 --> 01:04:24,168
Good job.

1781
01:04:24,308 --> 01:04:25,578
Yes.

1782
01:04:26,008 --> 01:04:27,178
Oishii.

1783
01:04:28,308 --> 01:04:29,908
By the way...

1784
01:04:29,948 --> 01:04:32,648
By the way, you need to keep the chopsticks balanced.

1785
01:04:32,718 --> 01:04:34,047
If one is too long, and the other is too short,

1786
01:04:34,048 --> 01:04:35,217
how are you going to grab food?

1787
01:04:35,218 --> 01:04:36,618
(The chopstick man is not easy to satisfy.)

1788
01:04:36,888 --> 01:04:38,188
Right? Try it now.

1789
01:04:38,488 --> 01:04:39,718
You know how to hold them at least.

1790
01:04:40,418 --> 01:04:43,328
Jjyu, I like that. You have to tell her every day.

1791
01:04:43,788 --> 01:04:46,457
Hold the chopsticks even when you're going to bed.

1792
01:04:46,458 --> 01:04:48,128
(Even before going to bed)

1793
01:04:48,268 --> 01:04:49,827
Then you can fix it.

1794
01:04:49,828 --> 01:04:51,798
(The chopstick man is persistent.)

1795
01:04:52,298 --> 01:04:54,767
Let's fix Woni and May's makeup.

1796
01:04:54,768 --> 01:04:55,808
Okay.

1797
01:04:56,338 --> 01:04:57,668
- But I just learned it. - Where?

1798
01:04:58,038 --> 01:04:59,577
- Yes. - You got it.

1799
01:04:59,578 --> 01:05:01,178
- That's good. - Good job.

1800
01:05:01,778 --> 01:05:03,207
- Yes. - You got it.

1801
01:05:03,208 --> 01:05:04,777
(Trying what she learned)

1802
01:05:04,778 --> 01:05:06,447
- You got it. - You did it.

1803
01:05:06,448 --> 01:05:07,548
Oishii.

1804
01:05:08,348 --> 01:05:10,118
Try it again after the shoot.

1805
01:05:10,418 --> 01:05:11,587
(Strict)

1806
01:05:11,588 --> 01:05:13,717
- Yes. - Or I'll take the food away.

1807
01:05:13,718 --> 01:05:14,788
Yes, sir!

1808
01:05:15,128 --> 01:05:16,257
See you later.

1809
01:05:16,258 --> 01:05:17,327
Thank you.

1810
01:05:17,328 --> 01:05:18,697
(The chopstick student leaves for the shoot.)

1811
01:05:18,698 --> 01:05:20,198
She has to practice.

1812
01:05:21,058 --> 01:05:24,198
Back in the military, I held the chopsticks for a week.

1813
01:05:24,998 --> 01:05:26,497
Because my girlfriend criticized me.

1814
01:05:26,498 --> 01:05:28,037
(Because my girlfriend criticized me)

1815
01:05:28,038 --> 01:05:30,868
(He was more scared of his girlfriend than the commander.)

1816
01:05:31,578 --> 01:05:33,008
You're different from me.

1817
01:05:33,278 --> 01:05:35,248
I fixed it right away after I got slapped in the face.

1818
01:05:36,648 --> 01:05:38,218
(That's how it was back then.)

1819
01:05:38,478 --> 01:05:39,517
It's cold.

1820
01:05:39,518 --> 01:05:41,687
(Taking a break while the studio is getting ready)

1821
01:05:41,688 --> 01:05:42,988
It's cold...

1822
01:05:43,048 --> 01:05:45,087
even if you turn off the AC in hotels.

1823
01:05:45,088 --> 01:05:46,288
(Copying Jjyu's pose)

1824
01:05:46,718 --> 01:05:47,987
(Spotting May)

1825
01:05:47,988 --> 01:05:49,728
(Smiling)

1826
01:05:50,388 --> 01:05:51,498
What?

1827
01:05:51,958 --> 01:05:53,228
- Jjyu. - Yes?

1828
01:05:53,298 --> 01:05:55,497
There's a place I want to go.

1829
01:05:55,498 --> 01:05:56,698
Where?

1830
01:05:57,568 --> 01:06:00,538
We have a little bit of time.

1831
01:06:01,338 --> 01:06:05,307
I want to go to a gacha store.

1832
01:06:05,308 --> 01:06:06,708
- What? - Gacha.

1833
01:06:07,638 --> 01:06:08,847
Do you know gacha?

1834
01:06:08,848 --> 01:06:09,948
The capsules.

1835
01:06:10,508 --> 01:06:12,077
- I heard it's crazy now. - I want to go there.

1836
01:06:12,078 --> 01:06:13,778
- Yes. Totally. - Right?

1837
01:06:13,848 --> 01:06:15,487
But it was popular in Japan.

1838
01:06:15,488 --> 01:06:16,717
- Yes. - Right?

1839
01:06:16,718 --> 01:06:18,518
I go to Japan for that.

1840
01:06:18,888 --> 01:06:20,887
I heard we have what Japan doesn't have.

1841
01:06:20,888 --> 01:06:21,888
(May also loves gacha.)

1842
01:06:21,889 --> 01:06:23,927
Anything you want, we'll make it true.

1843
01:06:23,928 --> 01:06:26,228
- Let's go! - Let's go.

1844
01:06:27,398 --> 01:06:30,068
(Woni, the gacha mate, joins after her shoot.)

1845
01:06:30,128 --> 01:06:31,598
- Nice. - Is it nearby?

1846
01:06:33,068 --> 01:06:34,598
Jjyu-Kkyu is the best.

1847
01:06:34,738 --> 01:06:35,767
You're even coming to...

