01:34:55,944 --> 01:34:57,353
(That's it!)

2628
01:34:57,354 --> 01:34:58,453
It's not oishii.

2629
01:34:58,454 --> 01:35:00,423
This one is a potato.

2630
01:35:00,424 --> 01:35:01,583
It feels good, right?

2631
01:35:01,584 --> 01:35:05,353
(The girls were happy with slime squishy and malatang.)

2632
01:35:05,354 --> 01:35:07,823
Were you happy when you moved to a bigger house?

2633
01:35:07,824 --> 01:35:08,993
I was so happy.

2634
01:35:08,994 --> 01:35:10,334
Oh, right there.

2635
01:35:10,964 --> 01:35:12,833
Oishii to okane.

2636
01:35:12,834 --> 01:35:15,233
(Awakened by the fallen secretary)

2637
01:35:15,234 --> 01:35:17,203
- You're on the right track. - I guess I had it pretty good.

2638
01:35:17,204 --> 01:35:18,233
Yes.

2639
01:35:18,234 --> 01:35:20,304
- Money is happiness. - It's not oishii.

2640
01:35:20,474 --> 01:35:21,603
- It's okane. - It's money.

2641
01:35:21,604 --> 01:35:22,644
(The dark capitalist instinct)

2642
01:35:23,144 --> 01:35:25,274
- Money. - That must be good, right?

2643
01:35:25,444 --> 01:35:27,613
People live for that.

2644
01:35:27,614 --> 01:35:28,684
- Right. - True.

2645
01:35:28,784 --> 01:35:30,614
You've already changed.

2646
01:35:31,384 --> 01:35:32,913
(Feeling proud)

2647
01:35:32,914 --> 01:35:33,953
Right?

2648
01:35:33,954 --> 01:35:36,223
Kkyu, is there anything you want to say?

2649
01:35:36,224 --> 01:35:38,054
What do you live for?

2650
01:35:38,094 --> 01:35:40,963
Once the first payment goes through,

2651
01:35:40,964 --> 01:35:42,624
a lot of scammers start coming after you.

2652
01:35:42,764 --> 01:35:43,963
Be careful.

2653
01:35:43,964 --> 01:35:45,293
(Tip: Watch out for scammers.)

2654
01:35:45,294 --> 01:35:46,363
- And... - And...

2655
01:35:46,364 --> 01:35:47,903
(I didn't want to learn the hard way.)

2656
01:35:47,904 --> 01:35:49,103
When you buy a house...

2657
01:35:49,104 --> 01:35:50,703
- Yes. - I love this.

2658
01:35:50,704 --> 01:35:52,204
Watch out for rental deposit scams.

2659
01:35:52,234 --> 01:35:53,274
That's right.

2660
01:35:53,434 --> 01:35:55,543
Watch out for rental deposit scams.

2661
01:35:55,544 --> 01:35:57,214
Don't use your registered seal without knowing what's going on.

2662
01:35:57,344 --> 01:35:58,413
- Right. - Okay?

2663
01:35:58,414 --> 01:36:00,143
Don't get a certificate of seal impression issued either.

2664
01:36:00,144 --> 01:36:02,214
- Make sure to check everything. - Okay.

2665
01:36:02,344 --> 01:36:05,454
(What are we telling the girls?)

2666
01:36:05,614 --> 01:36:09,054
Do you remember performing at an elementary school sports day?

2667
01:36:09,524 --> 01:36:11,424
- I do. - Of course, I do.

2668
01:36:11,624 --> 01:36:14,693
Because one of the students who was watching...

2669
01:36:14,694 --> 01:36:16,193
loved it so much that they cried.

2670
01:36:16,194 --> 01:36:17,463
- Right. - They had a light stick too.

2671
01:36:17,464 --> 01:36:18,533
Why did they cry?

2672
01:36:18,534 --> 01:36:20,764
- They knew who we were. - One of them knew.

2673
01:36:21,534 --> 01:36:23,004
You should perform at a bigger venue now.

2674
01:36:23,164 --> 01:36:24,974
- Right. - We should go to a bigger venue.

2675
01:36:25,134 --> 01:36:26,134
What are you going to do now?

2676
01:36:26,135 --> 01:36:28,403
(He suddenly sounds strict.)

2677
01:36:28,404 --> 01:36:30,713
(He's putting a lot of pressure on them.)

2678
01:36:30,714 --> 01:36:32,643
- We'll work really hard. - What?

2679
01:36:32,644 --> 01:36:34,043
- It won't work... - We'll work hard.

2680
01:36:34,044 --> 01:36:35,044
- if you touch slime squishies... - I'm sorry.

2681
01:36:35,045 --> 01:36:36,414
all the time.

2682
01:36:36,944 --> 01:36:38,283
(He talks like a true Thinker to the very end.)

2683
01:36:38,284 --> 01:36:40,113
- That's my small happiness, though. - It feels like you're scolding us.

2684
01:36:40,114 --> 01:36:41,284
- My gosh. - Sorry.

2685
01:36:41,754 --> 01:36:44,624
It's good to start from the bottom and work your way up.

2686
01:36:45,454 --> 01:36:48,364
Because it'll feel...

2687
01:36:48,624 --> 01:36:50,434
even more rewarding later.

2688
01:36:50,964 --> 01:36:54,033
People say, "Row while the tide is in."

2689
01:36:54,034 --> 01:36:56,204
Watching RESCENE,

2690
01:36:56,434 --> 01:36:58,874
I realized that they have literally...

2691
01:36:59,534 --> 01:37:02,173
been rowing nonstop...

2692
01:37:02,174 --> 01:37:04,244
toward their dreams.

2693
01:37:04,444 --> 01:37:07,514
And the tide came in at the perfect moment.

2694
01:37:08,814 --> 01:37:10,043
My Genie Secretary.

2695
01:37:10,044 --> 01:37:12,654
- Yaho. - Yaho.

2696
01:37:12,884 --> 01:37:14,253
- Yaho. - Thank you.

2697
01:37:14,254 --> 01:37:15,753
- You did a good job. - Thank you.

2698
01:37:15,754 --> 01:37:17,353
Well done.

2699
01:37:17,354 --> 01:37:18,994
- Thank you. - Thank you.

2700
01:37:19,918 --> 01:37:21,857
(Is there anything about My Star that you envy?)

2701
01:37:21,858 --> 01:37:22,888
(Wealth!)

2702
01:37:23,158 --> 01:37:24,627
(Which of you is wealthier?)

2703
01:37:24,628 --> 01:37:25,998
(I bet Jang Hoon is wealthier!)

2704
01:37:26,258 --> 01:37:27,468
You're not even trying to win.

2705
01:37:27,728 --> 01:37:29,997
(My star is so rich that even Young Master has to back down.)

2706
01:37:29,998 --> 01:37:32,598
(A billionaire)

2707
01:37:33,968 --> 01:37:35,768
(My Star, Seo Jang Hoon, the richest star on our show)

2708
01:37:35,938 --> 01:37:37,607
(Is it okay to spend up to 10,000 dollars on a get-together?)

2709
01:37:37,608 --> 01:37:38,637
(Yes)

2710
01:37:38,638 --> 01:37:39,778
Do you really spend that much on meals for everyone?

2711
01:37:40,548 --> 01:37:42,008
(Why did you put the building up for sale?)

2712
01:37:42,178 --> 01:37:44,378
(Are we finally going to find out about his 2 billion-dollar fortune?)

2713
01:37:44,548 --> 01:37:47,348
(And...)

2714
01:37:47,418 --> 01:37:49,247
(I want to see the combination of Lee Seo Jin and Seo Jang Hoon.)

2715
01:37:49,248 --> 01:37:51,088
(They're both such Thinkers.)

2716
01:37:51,758 --> 01:37:53,958
(Everyone has been waiting for this combination.)

2717
01:37:54,458 --> 01:37:56,258
(Seo Jin complains the most!)

2718
01:37:56,428 --> 01:37:58,358
(Lee Seo Jin, who is brutal with the facts)

2719
01:37:58,758 --> 01:38:01,068
(Jang Hoon is just as brutal!)

2720
01:38:01,368 --> 01:38:03,898
(Seo Jang Hoon, a master of sharp one-liners)

2721
01:38:04,068 --> 01:38:06,197
(Young Master...)

2722
01:38:06,198 --> 01:38:07,668
(versus Lord)

2723
01:38:07,968 --> 01:38:09,838
I'm a Thinker, but I have a warm heart.

2724
01:38:10,438 --> 01:38:12,008
He's a Thinker, and he's quite prickly.

2725
01:38:12,778 --> 01:38:14,048
(Jang Hoon wasn't like that back then.)

2726
01:38:14,748 --> 01:38:16,008
(This punk became a true entertainer.)

2727
01:38:16,308 --> 01:38:18,378
(A showdown between Thinkers)

2728
01:38:18,518 --> 01:38:21,718
(They have a long way to go while bickering. Will they be okay?)

2729
01:38:21,818 --> 01:38:23,918
(My Genie Secretary)
